Z||000000||jaguiler||06-21-2001||08:36 PM||||Hello everyone,<P>I was reading the search I did on overheating and I noticed that you guys rec. the un-vented rad cap.  I went to the stored and replaced mine with a Stant that looked just like mine, except mine said 16 pounds vented.  The new one did not mention vented, so I assuem it is unvented.<BR>My problem - it seems like my 2.8 keeps overhaeting.... last week it was doing it rapidly so I burped it...then everything was fine.  Now a days my running temp is fine but when I stop in traffic or when I get into town or let the car idle the temp slowly starts to creep towards 220....  <BR>After I park the car at that state I notice the coolant starts to overflow..... <BR>I burped the system today.... what I am I missing... my oil is clean, my coolant is clean... I have a new 'stat....<BR>What does the "burp" feel like.... or sound like?<P>Please help... thanks.....<P>------------------<BR><BR>______<BR>__|aguiler||65.8.46.102||reg||1
