Z||000009||cadaver||06-22-2001||12:23 AM||||I have used a manula vent cap for years. The one with the red lever. I have never had a problem and it makes it so easy to burp the air after I have worked on the system.||||reg||1
Z||000010||rogergarrison||06-22-2001||11:03 AM||||thats what i have too cadaver, on 3.1 and i havent had any problem in 4 years and 86K.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Seanh||06-22-2001||12:56 PM||||I had a bad overheating problem with my 3.4 GT about 2 months back. It kept puking up coolant after I shut it off. I was told to replace the rad. cap, so I went to NAPA and told them I needed a cap for an 86 Fiero. They gave me a vented one, and I was like this is the wrong one, I need non-vented. They said vented is what their system listed, and that the fact I had non-vented on there was probally the reason I was having trouble. I bought the vented one, and put it one. Iv driven it for 2 months and never had a problem since. I don't see any problem's in using a vented cap, yet....||||reg||1
Z||000012||theogre||06-22-2001||08:05 PM||||I covered this in my cave.<P>"Vented" will work as long as there is absolutly no way for air to get in the high end of the system. Unfortunatly it's all to easy to leak air into the system. (And do it w/o any apparent cooolant leak. Air doesn't need as big a hole as coolant does.)||||reg||1
